type: software
title: "PolyDrift: Differential Testing of Independent Protocol Implementations"
authors:
  - family-names: Kazuru
    given-names: Seke
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0002-4099-1059"
    email: kazuruuni@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
repository-code: "https://github.com/kazuru-chidumbwe/polydrift"
url: "https://github.com/kazuru-chidumbwe/polydrift"
abstract: >-
  PolyDrift sends the same input to several independent implementations of a
  protocol, records what each one does, and reports where they agree and where
  they differ. One observation model and one graded oracle serve six protocols
  in five cells: SIP proxies and registrars, DNS resolvers and forwarders, MQTT
  brokers, LDAP directory servers, and mail delivery and retrieval through Sieve
  and JMAP. Divergences are graded by their effect on a conforming consumer,
  and the grading is checked by replaying recorded responses into real client
  libraries.
keywords:
  - differential testing
  - test oracle
  - protocol implementations
  - interoperability
  - SIP
  - DNS
  - MQTT
  - LDAP
  - Sieve
